  {
   "id": "MeQgPafBAgAJ",
   "from": "Finn Lindgren",
   "author": "afb003e064114795",
   "date": "2020-09-21T12:18:31Z",
   "subject": "Re: [r-inla] LGCP in INLA and inlabru",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Two issues:<div>1)</div><div>You hadn&#39;t used the same control.inla settings for the lgcp() run.<div>You need to add<div>           options = list(control.inla = list(strategy = &quot;gaussian&quot;,<br>                                               int.strategy = &quot;eb&quot;)))<br></div></div><div>which gives roughly the same lgcp() hyperparameters as before, but different intercept estimate:</div><div>inla():</div><div>Intercept 3.010333 0.6024544   1.827512 3.010316   4.192167 3.010333   0<br></div><div>lgcp():</div><div>Intercept -1.408148 2.292181  -6.270027 -1.330071   3.083238 -1.186546 0.0007965716<br></div><div>lgcp() with inla options:</div><div>Intercept -0.2450238 1.75953  -3.699574 -0.2450733   3.206644 -0.2450238 3.586055e-17<br></div><div><br></div></div><div>2)</div><div>You constructed the LGCP sample on a [0,3] square, built the mesh larger to avoid boundary effects, and build the likelihood approximation for inla() on that [0,3] square, but you didn&#39;t tell lgcp() about it, so it tried to estimate lambda on the entire mesh.</div><div>Fixing this by specifying</div><div>  samplers = poly,</div><div>the result is much closer to the inla() result:</div><div><br></div><div>&gt; bru.fit$summary.hyperpar<br>                     mean        sd 0.025quant 0.5quant 0.975quant     mode<br>Range for mySPDE 1.509567 0.3809154  0.9363728 1.448457   2.420408 1.329187<br>Stdev for mySPDE 1.560258 0.3037610  1.0781074 1.519456   2.265846 1.433620<br>&gt; bru.fit$summary.fixed<br>              mean        sd 0.025quant 0.5quant 0.975quant     mode kld<br>Intercept 2.939428 0.5790095   1.802637 2.939412    4.07527 2.939428   0<br>.<br></div><div><br></div><div>The slight difference remaining is likely due to the different likelihood approximation method (the &quot;dual mesh counting&quot; is a slightly lower order integral approximation than the one used in inlabru).</div><div><br></div><div>Figure attached.</div><div><br></div><div>Finn</div><div><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Mon, 21 Sep 2020 at 11:12, Finn Lindgren &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">finn.l...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"auto\">Hi,<div><br></div><div>You’re using a different poisson process likelihood approximation for the plain inla() version, but I wouldn’t expect this big a difference in the results.</div><div>I’ll try to run your code later today.<br><br><div dir=\"ltr\">Finn</div><div dir=\"ltr\"><br><blockquote type=\"cite\">On 21 Sep 2020, at 10:48, Jorge Sicacha &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">jorges...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br><br></blockquote></div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div dir=\"ltr\">﻿<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial;float:none;display:inline\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial;float:none;display:inline\">Hi,</span></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\"><br></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\">I&#39;ve made a simple example for fitting the LGCP</div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\"><br></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\">log(lambda(s)) = beta_0 + w(s)</div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\"><br></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\">with w(s) a GRF with Matern covariance function.</div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\"><br></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\">Even if I fit the LGCP model using both INLA and inlabru R-packages using the same prior specification for w(s), I get very different results. See the attached figure (black line - posterior with INLA ; red line - posterior with inlabru; blue line - true value)</div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\"><br></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\"><div>&lt;Auto Generated Inline Image 1&gt;</div><br></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\"><br></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\">Is there any reason for these differences? I&#39;m quite new using inlabru and perhaps I&#39;ve made a mistake in my code (see attachments). Any help is really appreciated.</div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\"><br></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\">Best,</div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\"><br></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\">Jorge</div></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;R-inla discussion group&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">r-inla-discussion...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo view this discussion on the web, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/r-inla-discussion-group/e45666d6-e989-4e4c-a6f9-fc1218bb3e80o%40googlegroups.com?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=footer\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/r-inla-discussion-group/e45666d6-e989-4e4c-a6f9-fc1218bb3e80o%2540googlegroups.com?utm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dfooter&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=17924403158