    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Two issues:<div>1)</div><div>You hadn&#39;t used the same control.inla settings for the lgcp() run.<div>You need to add<div>           options = list(control.inla = list(strategy = &quot;gaussian&quot;,<br>                                               int.strategy = &quot;eb&quot;)))<br></div></div><div>which gives roughly the same lgcp() hyperparameters as before, but different intercept estimate:</div><div>inla():</div><div>Intercept 3.010333 0.6024544   1.827512 3.010316   4.192167 3.010333   0<br></div><div>lgcp():</div><div>Intercept -1.408148 2.292181  -6.270027 -1.330071   3.083238 -1.186546 0.0007965716<br></div><div>lgcp() with inla options:</div><div>Intercept -0.2450238 1.75953  -3.699574 -0.2450733   3.206644 -0.2450238 3.586055e-17<br></div><div><br></div></div><div>2)</div><div>You constructed the LGCP sample on a [0,3] square, built the mesh larger to avoid boundary effects, and build the likelihood approximation for inla() on that [0,3] square, but you didn&#39;t tell lgcp() about it, so it tried to estimate lambda on the entire mesh.</div><div>Fixing this by specifying</div><div>  samplers = poly,</div><div>the result is much closer to the inla() result:</div><div><br></div><div>&gt; bru.fit$summary.hyperpar<br>                     mean        sd 0.025quant 0.5quant 0.975quant     mode<br>Range for mySPDE 1.509567 0.3809154  0.9363728 1.448457   2.420408 1.329187<br>Stdev for mySPDE 1.560258 0.3037610  1.0781074 1.519456   2.265846 1.433620<br>&gt; bru.fit$summary.fixed<br>              mean        sd 0.025quant 0.5quant 0.975quant     mode kld<br>Intercept 2.939428 0.5790095   1.802637 2.939412    4.07527 2.939428   0<br>.<br></div><div><br></div><div>The slight difference remaining is likely due to the different likelihood approximation method (the &quot;dual mesh counting&quot; is a slightly lower order integral approximation than the one used in inlabru).</div><div><br></div><div>Figure attached.</div><div><br></div><div>Finn</div><div><br></div></div><br></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
